        "Integrate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 7 - x^2 - 6x$ to get $y = 7x - \\frac{1}{3}x^3 - 3x^2 + c$.",
        "Substitute $(3, -10)$ to find $c = 5$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate the derivative with respect to $x$:\n$$y = \\int (7 - x^2 - 6x)\\,dx = 7x - \\frac{1}{3}x^3 - 3x^2 + c$$",
        "Substitute the coordinates of the given point $(3, -10)$ to determine $c$:\n$$-10 = 7(3) - \\frac{3^3}{3} - 3(3^2) + c = 21 - 9 - 27 + c = -15 + c$$\n$$c = -10 + 15 = 5$$\n$$y = 7x - \\frac{1}{3}x^3 - 3x^2 + 5$$"
      ],
